# Astro's generated types and content cache. Regenerated on every build.
.astro/

# Cloudflare local state, if anyone runs `wrangler dev` in either Worker.
# It holds a local KV simulation, so after any real testing it contains actual
# submissions — names, phone numbers, messages. Never committed.
worker/.wrangler/
worker-demo/.wrangler/

# Deployment configs carrying real ids and addresses. The committed
# `wrangler.jsonc` next to each of these keeps its PLACEHOLDER values and stays
# the readable template; the real KV namespace id, MAIL_TO and origin list live
# here and are deployed with `wrangler deploy -c wrangler.local.jsonc`.
# Secrets are still never in any file — those are `wrangler secret put`.
worker/wrangler.local.jsonc
worker-demo/wrangler.local.jsonc

# `wrangler dev` reads secrets from `.dev.vars`. Ignored here so that a local
# Resend key used while exercising the form cannot be committed by accident.
# Deployed secrets are still `wrangler secret put` and live only in Cloudflare.
worker/.dev.vars
worker-demo/.dev.vars

# `dist/` is already covered by the root .gitignore.
